+90% or more is a copy". With that definition, §8's "New copies: none" holds for cross-file pairs
+only. The corrected statement:
+
+> **No new cross-file copies. 26 new in-file pairs at or above the 90% threshold, all between
+> sibling declarations of `ClassNP/ExhaustiveReplay.lean`, listed in §8 ("new pairs at 90% or
+> more: 26") and justified by family.**
+
+The 26 pairs (17 distinct declarations of the module's 185, 9.2%):
+- the twenty bank-distinctness one-liners `xr_*_ne_*` (92-97%);
+- `xr_testTM` / `xr_rewindTM` (94%), two leaf tables;
+- `xr_bufferTape_eq_none_iff` / `xr_bufferTape_ge` (93%);
